error[E0277]: the coefficients `[[f64; 6]; 4]` are not square: the map's input and output kinds have different sizes
 --> tests/compile_fail/solve_not_square.rs:5:15
  |
5 |     let _ = m.solve(b);
  |               ^^^^^ needs a map between kinds of the same size
  |
  = note: a map `B <- A` stores `[[T; size of A]; size of B]`; `inverse`, `solve`, `det`, `eigh`, `eig` and `svd` need the two sizes equal
  = note: for a map of another shape, `pinv()` is the pseudo-inverse, `lstsq(b)` the least-squares solution and `svd_thin()` the singular value decomposition
help: the trait `SquareArr<f64>` is not implemented for `[[f64; 6]; 4]`
      but it is implemented for `[[f64; 6]; 6]`
